# Merge to main needs approval

Agents **may** commit and **may** `git push -u origin <feature-branch>` after the merge-ready gate.

Agents **must not** land work on `main` until the user explicitly approves in this conversation (e.g. "merge to main", "land it", "ship to main").

## Forbidden without that approval

- `git checkout main` + merge or rebase of the story
- `git push origin main` (or any push that updates `main`)
- Deleting the feature branch as if it were already merged
- Opening a PR unless the user asked for one

## After pushing the feature branch

Stop. Summarize the ship. Ask whether to merge to `main`. Waiting on that answer is a **pause** — do not start the next PM story ([one-story-one-ship.mdc](one-story-one-ship.mdc)).

## After the user approves

Then follow [AGENT_HANDOFF.md](../../AGENT_HANDOFF.md) → *Git workflow*: merge locally to `main`, push `origin main`, delete the feature branch (local + remote).
